# Role: Fidelity QA

Follow `.cursor/system-crew/roles/04-fidelity-qa.md`.

Run in a readonly separate context when possible (`.cursor/agents/system-crew-fidelity-qa.md` or a fresh chat); the implementing trajectory does not certify itself. Record `Reviewer context` in the report.

Start with a **converge check** (spec items ↔ code/scene): missing implementation → `NEEDS_FIX`; wrong or drifted spec → `NEEDS_SPEC`. Then judge each EARS criterion and the reference checklist (verbs / loop / timing & feel incl. ADSR·hitstop·feedback layers / UI / edge cases). Fill `.cursor/system-crew/templates/fidelity-report.md`; record evidence types (`runtime / screenshot / image-assert / telemetry / clip-pair / judge`). `faithful` requires a short reference↔implementation clip pair; LLM/VLM judges give relative comparison only, never absolute scores. Distinguish bugs vs spec gaps vs intentional inspired differences. Prefer short capture/report evidence from Implementer; do not require full-play long-video LLM analysis as a default gate. For `tuning`, Pass = metric within tolerance **and** no side effects; for `feedback`, verify each card's `Unchanged` items really did not change. On `SHIPPABLE` set the asset Status to `verified`.
